# Patient data never enters git. External documents, images, e-mails and
# spreadsheets remain ignored; the reviewed Claude Design assets under
# design/ are the only intentional media exception.
# Every screen of Bridgr Pro shows a patient's name, so a real capture of the
# current app IS patient data. Mockups use the fictitious cast in
# docs/06-sample-data.md (AGENTS.md).
#
# The bracket patterns make the match case-insensitive: git's is not, and
# scanners and cameras write `.PDF` and `.JPG` all day.
#
# ⚠️ This guards the accident, never `git add -f` — the rule in AGENTS.md is
# broader than this list.
*.[pP][dD][fF]
*.[eE][mM][lL]
*.[mM][sS][gG]
*.[pP][nN][gG]
*.[jJ][pP][gG]
*.[jJ][pP][eE][gG]
*.[wW][eE][bB][pP]
*.[gG][iI][fF]
*.[tT][iI][fF]
*.[tT][iI][fF][fF]
*.[bB][mM][pP]
*.[hH][eE][iI][cC]
*.[xX][lL][sS]
*.[xX][lL][sS][xX]
*.[cC][sS][vV]
*.[oO][dD][sS]
*.[dD][oO][cC]
*.[dD][oO][cC][xX]
screenshots/
capturas/
documentos/

# Claude Design exports are kept under design/ as the reviewed visual artifact.
!*.dc.html
!design/uploads/
!design/uploads/*.png

# Local environment
.env
.env.*
